Z||000004||Fieroboy1||12-04-2000||06:37 PM||||what about the MAT sensor in the v/6 airbox?<BR>you'll have to relocate it if you remove the stock airbox.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||12-04-2000||09:04 PM||||The sensor can be placed in the tube????<P>What I want to know is will the guy at the smog station say anything about this type of set-up?? but with all the ones on the market<BR>I'm not sure they would even notice it?<P>But I heard others say keep the stock box and put it back on when time to smog.<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||12-04-2000||09:34 PM||||The question of the air box being taken out is not a problem. Yes you can take out the air box (The upsidedown water trap) with no problems with smog. No one would notice. Take out the air cleaner cannister? With all smog guys in my experience it depends. Some have looked right past the block off plate for the EGR valve without a glance. Another got antsy for the exhuast tips. Still others have simply gone in stuck the probe in the pipe and went back to watching television. Around here at least, we run the whole gambit. But they are starting to crack down a bit, I dont' have to go in until next year for my smog. <P>Bottom line around here in So Cal is this. You take your chances. It wouldn't hurt to keep it just in case you get Barney Fife for a smog guy. You don't have to put the water trap contraption on just the air canister for looks. Its easy.<P>(BTW that intake should come with a tap already installed for the sensor. $350? OUCH!)<P>Hope this helps and hope to seeya in July!<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 12-04-2000).]||||reg||6
